{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A watcher</b> — an angel. And Rabbi Moses said: it is not a body, and it is watchful continually and does not sleep." "<b>Came down</b> — descended. And like it: נחת גדודיה."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Rabbi Moses refers to R. Moses Ibn Ezra (or possibly Maimonides); resolved by inference from the philosophical content about incorporeality.", 1 "The quoted phrase נחת גדודיה is Aramaic ('her troops came down'), likely from the same verse or a related Aramaic usage; left untranslated as Ibn Ezra cites it without gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:48.933722574Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}